From: Monogram Desktop <monogram@neg-zero.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gpu: restore the previous clip after an unsuccessful first-node pass

The destination was reversed, leaving the processor clipped to the opaque
candidate even after restoring the scissor. Rounded popup content could lose
its top radius band for a frame while controls fade in or out.

Source: GNOME GTK 4.22.4, gsk/gpu/gskgpunodeprocessor.c
https://github.com/GNOME/gtk/blob/4.22.4/gsk/gpu/gskgpunodeprocessor.c
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later (upstream GTK)

--- a/gsk/gpu/gskgpunodeprocessor.c
+++ b/gsk/gpu/gskgpunodeprocessor.c
@@ -1436,7 +1436,7 @@ gsk_gpu_node_processor_add_first_node_clipped (GskGpuNodeProcessor   *self,
     }
 
   self->scissor = old_scissor;
-  gsk_gpu_clip_init_copy (&old_clip, &self->clip);
+  gsk_gpu_clip_init_copy (&self->clip, &old_clip);
 
   return FALSE;
 }
